The book's text around it: ‘Rickshaw Puller’, woodcut by Lan Jia. The novel Rickshaw by Lao She (1936) became a classic. The Guomindang despite its attempts to unite the country failed because of its narrow social base and limited political vision. A major plank in Sun Yat-sen’s programme – regulating capital and equalising land – was never carried out because the party ignored the peasantry and the rising social inequalities. It sought to impose military order rather then address the problems faced by the people. The story of rising prices. TIMELINE

